# Linux systemd and nginx lab

## What I practiced

- Checked Linux system information
- Installed nginx
- Managed nginx with systemctl
- Checked service status
- Read service logs with journalctl
- Tested nginx with curl
- Intentionally broke nginx configuration and fixed it

## Commands

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nginx -y
systemctl status nginx
curl localhost
sudo systemctl stop nginx
sudo systemctl start nginx
sudo systemctl restart nginx
sudo systemctl enable nginx
journalctl -u nginx --no-pager
```

## Nginx test page

```bash
echo "<h1> Artur Devops Lab</h1>" | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html
curl localhost
```

Result:

```html
<h1> Artur Devops Lab</h1>
```

## Troubleshooting nginx

I intentionally broke nginx configuration by adding an invalid directive:

```nginx
wrong_directive on;
```

Then I tested the configuration:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

The error was:

```text
unknown directive "wrong_directive" in /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default:47
nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test failed
```

Then restart failed:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

I checked logs:

```bash
journalctl -u nginx -xe | tail -20
```

After removing the invalid directive, I tested again:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

Result:

```text
nginx: the configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf syntax is ok
nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test is successful
```

## What I learned

- `nginx -t` checks configuration before restarting the service.
- `systemctl restart nginx` fails if nginx config has syntax errors.
- `journalctl` helps debug failed services.
- Error messages often show the exact file and line number.
- A DevOps engineer should know how to break, diagnose and fix services.
